 the body. Conversely, high amounts of garlic can reduce the absorption of Saquinavir, potentially diminishing its effectiveness.", "NELFINAVIR:Nelfinavir es un antirretroviral que puede estar relacionado con la producción de diarrea.", "LOPINAVIR:Lopinavir es un antirretroviral que puede causar diarrea como efecto secundario.)<|COMPLETE|>", "ENFERMEDAD DE CHAGAS:Enfermedad infecciosa causada por el parásito Trypanosoma cruzi, que afecta principalmente a personas en América Latina", "ENFERMEDAD NEUROLÓGICA:\"ENFERMEDAD NEUROLÓGICA\" refers to a broad category of disorders that impact the brain, spinal cord, and nerves. These neurological diseases can result in a range of complications, including dysphagia (difficulty swallowing) and malnutrition, highlighting the significant effects these conditions can have on an individual's overall health and well-being.", "ENFERMEDAD ENDOCRINA:Disorders that affect the endocrine system, leading to hormonal imbalances", "PANHIPOPITUITARISMO:A rare disorder in which the pituitary gland fails to produce sufficient amounts of several hormones", "DISTRÓFIA MIOTÓNICA:A genetic disorder that affects muscle function and can lead to progressive muscle weakness", "ESCLEROSIS SISTÉMICA:A chronic autoimmune disease that causes the skin and connective tissues to become thick and hard", "NADYA:NADYA is a comprehensive group dedicated to the study and support of artificial nutrition, specifically focusing on home and outpatient settings in Spain. The group is involved in both home parenteral nutrition and home enteral nutrition, with a particular emphasis on patients suffering from neurological diseases. Since its establishment in 1992, NADYA has maintained a registry that collects and reports data on patients receiving home parenteral nutrition (NPD), as well as on complications related to enteral nutrition. Through its efforts, NADYA aims to enhance nutritional support and improve outcomes for patients requiring specialized nutritional care.